    "reading": {
        "body": "Cryptography hiring in this sample is concentrated in a handful of employers, with IonQ alone accounting for four of eight postings, all in Geneva.\n\nThe pattern is narrow and specific. IonQ's four roles span distinguished, principal, staff, and senior levels, which suggests a team being built rather than a single seat filled. ServiceNow contributes three postings, two of them identical senior platform cryptography roles split between Santa Clara and San Diego. Cloudflare adds one PKI and cryptographic systems role. Every posting is tagged security and cryptography, and the dates cluster tightly between September 28 and October 2, 2026.\n\nFor AI specifically, this data says little directly. Cryptography underpins secure inference, model weight protection, and attestation for distributed training, but none of these postings name AI workloads, GPUs, data centers, or power. IonQ is a quantum computing company, and post-quantum cryptography work is adjacent to AI security rather than downstream of compute scaling. The Geneva concentration reflects one employer's hiring geography, not a broader European trend.\n\nWhat this does not cover is volume. Eight postings across three companies is a snapshot, not a labor market. The source list includes large aggregators, but the returned results come mostly from a single European board and two company career pages, so absence of other employers here is not evidence they are not hiring. Nothing in the data connects these roles to buildings, grid capacity, or compute supply.",
